t venom in the mcu  but as we know from the morbius trailer  venom is kind of already starting to  bleed into the spider verse of the mcu  and spider-man is kind of bleeding into  sony's spider-verse as well  so sony and marvel are starting to  really play nice with each other so this  doesn't come as that big of a surprise  now for those of you who are not aware  of who agent venom is and who anti-venom  is don't worry i'll explain  in the comics flash thompson who we've  also seen in the spider-man homecoming  films  goes from picking on peter parker and  being his bully to actually becoming  quite close with him  he would end up joining the military but  unfortunately he would end up losing  both of his legs to war  but he ends up regaining his legs thanks  to an experiment where he bonds with the  venom symbiote flash would end up  being able to control the venom symbiote  using some drugs and he would go on to  become  agent venom doing good fighting for the  military  and something that him and eddie brock  have in common is that they've both been  the host of venom  and anti-venom anti-venom actually  started when eddie brock separated from  the venom symbiote eddie would end up  later on getting cancer but he was  cured by martin lee the alter ego of the  super villain mr negative  he used his powers to heal eddie but in  the process he accidentally infused the  remnants of the symbiote in eddie's  bloodstream with his power  and ended up fusing the remnants of the  venom symbiote with his white blood  cells  this created a new kind of hybrid  symbiote and the new symbiote came out  when  venom tried to reattach to eddie brock  eddie would end up calling this new  symbiote anti-venom as it had some very  specific powers that the venom symbiote  did not have  including producing antibodies that can  cure any known disease and remove  any other impurities within a human body  but the main difference between the  anti-venom symbiote and any other  symbiote out 